{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21f87e39d99b57bc5b86", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "d and f Block Elements - Test 5", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 37, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c328"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c2e1", "title": "Chemistry Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c26b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205c0"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f45"], "concepts": ["6117b96e67dbe2603c3e9e62"], "question": {"text": "Among the following, which is the strongest oxidizing agent?"}, "options": [{"id": "ba16a1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Mn</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c26c"}, {"id": "5e487a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ti</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c26d"}, {"id": "8f792f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c26e"}, {"id": "7875a8", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cr</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c26f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c270", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205c0"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b73"], "concepts": ["60d3035daf049203d853666b"], "question": {"text": "Potassium permanganate on heating at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>513</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> gives a product which is :"}, "options": [{"id": "defbe8", "text": "paramagnetic and colourless", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c271"}, {"id": "11e557", "text": "diamagnetic and colourless", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c272"}, {"id": "2b68c3", "text": "diamagnetic and green", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c273"}, {"id": "55ec2b", "text": "paramagnetic and green", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c274"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c275", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205c0"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b478a"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b474b"], "question": {"text": "<p>The incorrect statement(s) among (a) - (c) is (are) :</p><p>(a) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>VI</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is more stable than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cr</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>VI</mi><mo>)</mo></math>.</p><p>(b) in the presence of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCl</mi></math>, permanganate titrations provide satisfactory results.</p><p>(c) some lanthanoid oxides can be used as phosphors</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "c5a3eb", "text": "(b) and (c) only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c276"}, {"id": "43a4aa", "text": "(a) and (b) only&nbsp;", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c277"}, {"id": "bd4fa4", "text": "(b) only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c278"}, {"id": "49487b", "text": "(a) only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c279"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c27a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205c0"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f45"], "concepts": ["60e567ab499d1e49588f95dc"], "question": {"text": "Consider ' $n$ ' is the number of lone pair of electrons present in the equatorial position of the most stable structure of $\\mathrm{ClF}_3$. The ions from the following with ' $n$ ' number of unpaired electrons are\nA. $\\mathrm{V}^{3+}$\nB. $\\mathrm{Ti}^{3+}$\nC. $\\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}$\nD. $\\mathrm{Ni}^{2+}$\nE. $\\mathrm{Ti}^{2+}$\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below:"}, "options": [{"id": "247481", "text": "A and C Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c27b"}, {"id": "c019f6", "text": "A, D and E Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c27c"}, {"id": "0076a4", "text": "B and D Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c27d"}, {"id": "072fc8", "text": "B and C Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c27e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c27f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205c0"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b73"], "concepts": ["6162fbe76ed13040ec8545c3"], "question": {"text": "Given below are two statements :\nStatement (I) : Fusion of \\(\\mathrm{MnO}_2\\) with \\(\\mathrm{KOH}\\) and an oxidising agent gives dark green \\(\\mathrm{K}_2 \\mathrm{MnO}_4\\).\nStatement (II) : Manganate ion on electrolytic oxidation in alkaline medium gives permanganate ion.\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "9a2098", "text": "Statement I is true but Statement II is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c280"}, {"id": "8e0094", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c281"}, {"id": "6c0518", "text": "Statement I is false but Statement II is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c282"}, {"id": "774ab4", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c283"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c284", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205c0"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b478a"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4742"], "question": {"text": "<p>Which one amongst the following are good oxidising agents?</p><p>(a)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Sm</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math></p><p>(b)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ce</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math></p><p>(c)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ce</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math></p><p>(d)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Tb</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "fcdb85", "text": "C only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c285"}, {"id": "65ca6c", "text": "D only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c286"}, {"id": "4ac34e", "text": "A and B only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c287"}, {"id": "c8be51", "text": "C and D only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c288"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c289", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205c0"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f45"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52be"], "question": {"text": "Consider the hydrated ions of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> . The correct order of their spin-only magnetic moments is:"}, "options": [{"id": "cb03ea", "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c28a"}, {"id": "e0e091", "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c28b"}, {"id": "a55ba7", "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c28c"}, {"id": "0e09c7", "text": "<math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c28d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c28e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205c0"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b73"], "concepts": ["60da9e95bce5511ac09ad9b3"], "question": {"text": "In chromyl chloride test for confirmation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cl</mi><mo>–</mo></msup></math> ion, a yellow solution is obtained. Acidification of the solution and addition of amyl alcohol and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo><mo> </mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo> </mo></math>turns organic layer blue indicating formation of chromium pentoxide. The oxidation state of chromium in that is"}, "options": [{"id": "21c3ee", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c28f"}, {"id": "dbe856", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c290"}, {"id": "bd3f40", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c291"}, {"id": "ac4965", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c292"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c293", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205c0"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b478a"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b474b"], "question": {"text": "Which one of the following lanthanoids does not form <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>MO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>? [<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> is lanthanoid metal]"}, "options": [{"id": "02bb19", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Yb</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c294"}, {"id": "2819cc", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Dy</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c295"}, {"id": "47e7b4", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Nd</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c296"}, {"id": "a1d82e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Pr</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c297"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1c2ee0e063d923c298", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205c0"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f45"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f18"], "question": {"text": "The first transition s